TRUE — For a binomial distribution:

- if $p < 1/2$, the mass concentrates on the left and the right tail is longer (right-skewed);
- if $p > 1/2$, the mass concentrates on the right and the left tail is longer (left-skewed);
- if $p = 1/2$, it is symmetric.

Here $p = 2/3 > 1/2$, so the distribution is left-skewed.
